  "callouts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "section": 1,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "Neither \\(A\\subseteq B\\) nor \\(B\\subseteq A\\). A single subgroup\nchain cannot contain both. We will construct two refinements and match their\nfactors.",
      "htmlSha256": "44b88d003f337fbeb9f312ceec90543a52b53aaeec7b331fd0192c0f127d9d4f"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "section": 1,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Main route: \\mainref{3}{main §3}, the general refinement theorem,\nand \\mainref{4-4}{main §4.4}, the \\(C_6\\) comparison.",
      "htmlSha256": "0bccaf2df4d6ae17b88080b236e85c446f98458147177cb00e4939922ce603b7"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "section": 2,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "Why does \\(x+A\\mapsto x\\) fail to define a map \\(G/A\\to G\\)?\nCompare the representatives \\(0\\) and \\(3\\).",
      "htmlSha256": "ea43989b0453fd993c257ead9d1affa0144a98d8be1f5e4c2978048197b83313"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "section": 2,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Further development: \\mainref{1}{main §1}, relations, images and quotients.",
      "htmlSha256": "2edf9277217e5e7c1e76cb9bb9ef31880aea4e1b43f698e9e7b8cb82abcbaf94"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "section": 3,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "The three-corner property does not require a unique output.\nIt says that three corners of a related rectangle force the fourth.",
      "htmlSha256": "a521fb611493e221d76d385f810b57a8bda8012700e2bffc85524140e56f90d4"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "section": 3,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Main §§1--2 develop the same operations using pullbacks, regular\nimages and effective quotients, so that they apply beyond groups.",
      "htmlSha256": "fbaa59134ee596cf3adea3dac92af0a908feeb9d42dada897d7c83e93c5bda43"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "section": 4,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "The pair \\((2,5)\\) belongs to \\(R\\). Does \\((5,2)\\)?\nKeep input support and output support separate.",
      "htmlSha256": "548a89fb00d1cc5f1a8a7d097c266a68761df90ef459dfb4176fcd1c723972e2"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "section": 4,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "This is the concrete instance of the common-quotient construction\nin \\mainref{2}{main §2}.",
      "htmlSha256": "afe531ee2bba7ab5ca1d088366bb805481a478da42ac23e23dc8a05872f15421"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "section": 5,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "The conclusion is an isomorphism characterized by a commuting\ndiagram, not merely equality of the numbers of classes.",
      "htmlSha256": "c0967b67fdf04cf1aba5d035197b1bc122f743ac88ddd4fb47ec1e892bf01bd7"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "section": 5,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "This page proves the group mechanism. The proof for every exact\nMal'cev category, with its image and quotient dependencies, is in\n\\mainref{1}{main §1} and \\mainref{2}{main §2}.",
      "htmlSha256": "bdbd51628da4abb85e35a43fd181a16476789d64717b1e9e056449a7c9fad931"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "section": 6,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "A zero entry is the one-element group. It does not mean that\nthe relation is empty, or even that its support is small.",
      "htmlSha256": "e1ce5851f8d9b9e0549159b33b3506ce323ee88923f30b2863a0397b522567d4"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "section": 7,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "For the categorical descent and boundary checks, see\n\\mainref{2}{main §2} and \\mainref{3}{main §3}.",
      "htmlSha256": "7afbac60242774f8454894e6cf964ce796f864e1765050c4ef748577328ddfc8"
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "section": 8,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "This is a complete stopping point for the teaching route.\nThe higher chapters ask what the list of factors forgets, and what extra\nstructure can retain or recover that information.",
      "htmlSha256": "a647674598ce72e97cbd43d8cf22dd34e1d2a285ed93db21378b10c38d2c032a"
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "section": 9,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Read this after the concrete rectangle. It is an abelian\n\\(\\Z\\)-module calculation; it does not assert that ordinary abelian\nspectral sequences apply directly to arbitrary groups.",
      "htmlSha256": "ad3b4dc35669b7e1631c4f2ba3daf45bad42bbfc4ac6ed83a20d99e23f75d790"
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "section": 10,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Exercises 1--5 check the comparison mechanism. Exercises 6--7\nexpose two features deliberately invisible in the easy \\(C_6\\) example:\nnon-ambient normality and different ways to assemble the same factors.",
      "htmlSha256": "c498c9be30ba09e146db2126875b8b0807a56e655efc2d81e8eebb14aa3f466c"
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "section": 11,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "The ternary expression \\(uv^{-1}w\\) need not be a group\nhomomorphism in its three variables. The proof uses closure of the\nsubgroup under the displayed operations, not such a homomorphism claim.",
      "htmlSha256": "f8358781be11d761b3ab37492e34007645c2eae65dc4db9fbe6caa864fbd51c4"
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "section": 12,
      "kind": "pausehere",
      "raw": "At each stage ask which object is being used. The orbit set\nforgets stabilizers; the action groupoid and its classifying homotopy\n\\(1\\)-type retain equivalent information.",
      "htmlSha256": "4a972f972ff2f37da1d01c7dd9526f17ef870ffc414509a822340e103485595f"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "section": 12,
      "kind": "route",
      "raw": "Further reading: \\href{https://tensorgami.com/notes/quotients-and-reconstruction.html}\n{Quotients, Refinement and Reconstruction};\n\\href{https://tensorgami.com/notes/quotients-and-reconstruction-audit.html}\n{notes on proofs, dependencies, and revisions}.",
      "htmlSha256": "70bd32ac2c3728b2c638f83ac55fe4f3cf1fb6dcf4a19e12ef12e448c2a379b6"
    }
  ],
